  "sections": {
    "work": [
      {
        "kind": "quote",
        "text": "The subject matter and composition are unusual, with six studies of heads crammed in a small space, distributed in three groups of two, all lit by a light source at the upper left.",
        "source": {
          "author": "Wikipedia contributors",
          "title": "Hogarth's Servants",
          "readAt": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hogarth%27s_Servants",
          "accessed": "2026-11-04",
          "tier": 5,
          "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0"
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "quote",
        "text": "By some they were said to be nature itself, by others declared most execrable ; so that time only can decide whether I was the best or the worst face painter of my day ; for a medium was never so much as suggested.",
        "source": {
          "author": "William Hogarth",
          "title": "Autobiographical notes, in Anecdotes of William Hogarth, Written by Himself",
          "publisher": "J. B. Nichols and Son",
          "year": "1833",
          "readAt": "https://archive.org/stream/anecdotesofwilli00hoga/anecdotesofwilli00hoga_djvu.txt",
          "accessed": "2026-11-04",
          "tier": 1,
          "license": "Public domain"
        },
        "lead": "Hogarth on his own portraits:"
      }
    ],
    "moment": [
      {
        "kind": "quote",
        "text": "Hogarth is exploring the differences of human physiognomy as he had in his print Characters and Caricaturas of 1743.",
        "source": {
          "author": "Wikipedia contributors",
          "title": "Hogarth's Servants",
          "readAt": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hogarth%27s_Servants",
